                  <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_Eng_hist_c_36-item1">
                     <rubric>The pope sente by a prothonotary the hate appertening for the high honor and dignitie of a cardinall vnto the most reuerend father in God lord
 Thomas Wulcy archebishopp of Yorke.</rubric>
                     <rubric>In the yere of our lord a Ml. vc. xv the xv day of November beinge Thuresday and the vijth yere of our souerain lord
                        King Henry the Eight the ſaid prothonotary entred into London whiche before according was mett bothe at the see side, lykewise at
                        Cantorbury and at Rochestre with the bishop of the same</rubric>
                     <explicit defective="true">before the mydle of the high aultre where for a certayn tyme he lay grovely</explicit>
                     <note>An account of the delivery by a papal protonotary to <persName key="person_22937889">Thomas Wolsey</persName> of the cardinal's hat in 1515.</note>
                     <listBibl><bibl>Pr. from a manuscript in the College of Arms in Richard Fiddes, <title>The life of Cardinal Wolsey</title> (1724), Appendix, pp. 251-3; the text here breaking off imperfect p. 252 l. 18 from bottom.</bibl></listBibl>
                     <textLang mainLang="en">English</textLang>
                  </msItem>
